  "text": "Done. The page is shared with you and Blake: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1QiVAgN3d3XDfJvLp_dJWkNLicxmk9ycFkSJU9f-ygno/edit\n\n**Cost to build** (Deel team + studios/freelancers, from the SVB notices Sep 2023 to Feb 2, split by transaction date):\n• Domino Delights: **$951,817.64**\n• ZM: **$544,433.44**\n• Combo Fighter: **$72,685.61**\n\n**What each brought in** (lifetime revenue, warehouse REVENUE_DAILY):\n• Domino Delights: **$12,331.25**\n• ZM: **$11.99**\n• Combo Fighter: left off for now, as you asked\n\n**Changes on the draft deck**\n• Slide 3 (\"What each bet cost to build\"): DD $985K → **$952K**, ZM $609K → **$544K**, CF $74K → **$73K**\n• Slide 4 (\"What each brought in\", now \"to fill in\"): DD **$12.3K**, ZM **$12**. No CF figure\n\n**Why it differs from your quick pass:** your pass counted every USD notice. I took these out of build cost:\n• Marketing: DD $16,428.57 (Node Media), ZM $56,537.06 (Adjoe, AppLovin, PlayableX, Telegram UA), CF $1,000. These are still listed under each bet on the sheet\n• Company: $49,625 (Singular, TYZ, trademarks, JP's website, the 4X help). Martin's laptop was paid in BGN 1,999, so it stays in BGN and isn't added to any total\n• $4,000 to JPMorgan ***3203 (Aug 2024) went to our own Chase account (Blake confirmed), so $0\n• Oleg's $125 wire came back. There's no Payoneer receipt in my mail, so $0\n• The Apr 2024 $4,032 MotMot wire to ***8605 came back, so that one is out\n• Leapblock's own close-out says they got $407,944 over 30 wires. The notices miss their first wire ($33,290, Sep 13, 2023), so their line uses the close-out figure\n\nAll 22 payee issues in Linear are Done, with a note first on the four where my figure isn't what the notices add up to (Leapblock, MotMot, Oleg, JPMorgan)."
 }
